00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.820
barren plain the wind swept

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:08.310
a small bird. The old man spilled crumbs from his sandwich onto the ground. The bird ate the crumbs

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:20.070
and perched to sing in the branches of a tin tree. The next morning, the visitor was gone.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:27.220
All day, the old man walked through the silence, and his heart ached with emptiness.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.380
That night, by moonlight, he made a wish.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.140
Woke to the sound of birdsong.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:47.340
The visitor had returned, and his mate had come with him.

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:50.350
The birds carried seeds in their beaks.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.800
They dropped them to the dry ground.

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:56.090
Green shoots broke through the earth.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:05:59.980
Soon the soil had returned.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.180
A song of birds mingled with the buzzing of insects and the rustle of leaves.

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:13.920
Small creatures appeared, creeping among the forest of trees.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:18.450
Wild animals slipped through the green shadows.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:29.970
It was once a forest near no...

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:36.180
aware and close to forgotten, that was filled with all the things that everyone wanted.

